        "text": "method",
        "refs": ["Q0008", "Q0009", "Q0010"],
        "claims": [
          {
            "text": "A method is a function that is part of a class.",
            "basis": "explicit",
            "availability": "SOURCE_SUPPORTED",
            "literal_kind": "verbal",
            "instructional_role": "prerequisite",
            "refs": ["Q0009"],
            "related_refs": []
          },
          {
            "text": "Methods are the functions defined inside the curly braces of a class.",
            "basis": "explicit",
            "availability": "SOURCE_SUPPORTED",
            "literal_kind": "verbal",
            "instructional_role": "prerequisite",
            "refs": ["Q0008"],
            "related_refs": []
          },
          {
            "text": "In languages like Python a function can exist outside a class, but when it belongs to a class it is called a method.",
            "basis": "explicit",
            "availability": "SOURCE_SUPPORTED",
            "literal_kind": "verbal",
            "instructional_role": "explanation_of_mistake",
            "refs": ["Q0010"],
            "related_refs": []
          }
        ]
      },
      "definition_text": {
        "text": "A method is a function that belongs to a class; it is defined inside the class’s curly braces, and unlike standalone functions in some languages, methods are associated with the class they reside in.",
